        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "a8e1fea4-9579-56d5-8c27-3fd793113ca8",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Companies: ValuJet Airlines\n- Events: ValuJet Flight 592 crash\n- Places: Miami, Everglades, Clayton County, Georgia, Eastern United States, Canada\n- Products: McDonnell-Douglas DC-9\n\nFacts:\n- During the 1990s, ValuJet Airlines was an American low-cost carrier headquartered in unincorporated Clayton County, Georgia, and it operated regularly scheduled domestic and international flights in the Eastern United States and Canada.\n- On May 11, 1996, ValuJet Flight 592, a ValuJet Airlines McDonnell-Douglas DC-9 operating from Miami, crashed into the Everglades about 11 minutes after takeoff.\n- The crash of ValuJet Flight 592 was caused by a fire in the cargo compartment that resulted from improperly stored cargo.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "0c263a15-20a7-53d6-9b25-d4d612f034c7",
